<title>MEXICO: Mexico's bolsa to trade Brady, other bonds.</title>
<headline>Mexico's bolsa to trade Brady, other bonds.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's stock exchange will allow secondary trading in various Mexican government bonds later this month, newspapers reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The trading will include Brady bonds as well as long term debt from the United Mexican States, the formal name of the federal government, Mexican Antonio del Valle, president of the Mexican Banker's Association, said in a press conference on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Finance Ministry deputy minister Martin Werner said the secondary market trading will involve debt worth $30.15 billion, El Economista newspaper reported.</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 7902))</p>
